# builtin-is-contractive returns true for a TypeNode.Union variant with no payload.
# The Union/Intersect branch (Case 3) tries to inspect the `types` child Seq.
# When the payload is absent (unit variant), it cannot be inspected — the algorithm
# returns true conservatively: "no self-references we can see = trivially contractive".
# This is a robustness property: malformed or incomplete TypeNode values never
# incorrectly trigger a contractiveness rejection.
[union-node: [builtin-variant "TypeNode.Union"]]
[result: [builtin-is-contractive union-node]]
